WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.100
It starts with the use-case inventory,
the one AI list every agency keeps.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.408
Read as identity data, it
gives you a stable ID,

3
00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:13.325
an office and a lifecycle stage,
where retired means a leaver event.

4
00:00:13.325 --> 00:00:18.400
It leaves blank everything that decides
what an AI system can touch: the account

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.013
it signs in as, its credential, its
permissions and its accountable owner.

6
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:25.624
And its high-impact fields report status.

7
00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:31.025
They say yes or in progress; they don't
carry a log, a document or a name.

8
00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:32.987
So treat it as the seed list.

9
00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:36.915
The decision belongs to the
Chief AI Officer: no use case is

10
00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:41.662
recorded as piloted or deployed
without a link to its identity record.

11
00:00:41.662 --> 00:00:43.660
Next, what kind of identity.
